id: pm-context-kzoe
title: Return smallest cited witnesses for contradictory context claims
description: ""
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-23T14:30:51.600Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T15:32:53.720Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Conflicting state, supersession and mutually exclusive policy fixtures produce stable witnesses; no automatic edits or unsupported semantic certainty. Typed SDK and CLI, bounded JSON and TOON, actionable refusals, non-git read-only public tracker validation, CRLF file-focus regression, npm and Bun CI release gates."
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T14:31:23.193Z",codex-agent,"Overlap checked against the installed CLI SDK context packing and relationship history contracts plus sibling README surfaces: core owns tracker reads, citations and selection; pm-memory owns durable consolidation and lexical or semantic proposals; pm-jev owns typed model decisions. No smallest packet contradiction witness API found. Implement explicit producer-declared state, policy and supersession claims with citation coordinates; deterministic smallest witnesses only, no inference, source edits or model calls. Reuse SDK expected errors, existing bounded JSON input reader and complete item reader for validation. Include CRLF focus fix and behavioral revert proofs. Local targeted tests/typecheck/docstring; CI npm and Bun full gates at existing thresholds."
  "2026-10-23T14:36:36.653Z",codex-agent,"Live overlap refresh used CLI 2026.10.23 context packing declarations as well as the package-pinned 2026.10.20 SDK. Core graph governance checks storage/ordering contradictions and bounded graph witnesses, not co-current assertion values. Packing lineage suppresses superseded duplicates but does not return packet inconsistency witnesses. This feature retains selection ownership in the existing context packer and checks only supplied declarations; citation locations are producer-owned, not independent source verification."
  "2026-10-23T14:43:27.592Z",codex-agent,"Public-data measurement used the committed public pm-context tracker at base fed1f6d, exported without Git metadata. The owned copy was made read-only and read with no Git executable on PATH: 87 items selected, 925 history entries inspected, 181 source files byte-identical afterward. Current-only: 87 claims, 0 conflicts, 270 JSON bytes/261 TOON bytes, 123.65 ms. Reusing 82 real historical status assertions as co-current (deliberate stale handoff assembly): 169 claims, 82 conflicting pairs, smallest witness size 2, 691 JSON bytes/773 TOON bytes, 125.73 ms. Reversed inputs give identical reports. Item read/selection took 4594.17 ms under host load. Historical overlay is a validation scenario, not a claim of 82 corrupt source items."
  "2026-10-23T14:46:57.397Z",codex-agent,"Linked pm test run: node --test --test-name-pattern=stable test/witnesses.test.ts passed 3/3 via pm test --run --progress --only-last --workspace-context source --pm-context schema --override-linked-workspace-context --override-linked-pm-context. The tracker has test-result recording disabled; no setting was changed. Source typecheck and docstring lint passed; test typecheck found an unused type import, which was removed, and the rerun passed. No dedicated eslint script exists; docstring is the repository lint gate."
  "2026-10-23T14:48:45.552Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: bypassing only conflict detection in checkContextWitnesses makes the stable state/policy/supersession fixtures fail 3/3 (0 pass, exit 1); restoring detection returns the linked run to 3/3 pass. Removing only the trailing newline normalization from normalizeFocusPath makes the new edited-file-list regression fail 1/1 (exit 1). Mutations were restored in finally blocks; no history or external source was altered. Tests import the changed source helpers directly; installed CLI checks use the rebuilt distribution."
  "2026-10-23T14:50:38.141Z",codex-agent,"Targeted new-module coverage reached 100% lines/branches/functions. The broad focused run passed 39/40; its failing assertion incorrectly required the entire host error envelope to omit invocation paths. Inspection confirmed the package detail/next_steps are path-free, while the host appends normalized arguments and refusal metadata. Updated the assertion to enforce the package-owned boundary and documented the host behavior. Observed CLI UX gap: an invalid format is assigned refusal.surface=--packet and rejected_value=packet argument instead of the actual invalid format; retained for final reporting, no upstream issue filed."
  "2026-10-23T14:53:07.778Z",codex-agent,"Final focused witness suite passed 9/9 with 100% new-module lines/branches/functions. All 24 file-focus and 7 renderer tests passed in the focused file run; the updated registration/CRLF/renderer selection passed 5/5. CRLF-first revert proof specifically observed src/one.ts with a retained CRLF: 0/1 pass, exit 1, then restored. Build, source/test typechecks and docstring lint passed. Final no-Git public runner recheck: 87 items, 925 events, 181 unchanged files; current-only 87 claims/0 conflicts/270 JSON bytes/261 TOON bytes/18.89 ms; stale-history overlay 169 claims/82 pairs/witness size 2/691 JSON bytes/773 TOON bytes/61.29 ms; read/selection 2912.54 ms. CI npm and Bun release gates will supply the full-suite evidence at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-23T14:59:18.118Z",codex-agent,"Ready PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/pull/168 . First CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/39973734387 at eaa08c1 passed all 403 tests in both Node 22 and 26 jobs, plus strict tracker health/typecheck/docstring/build-drift checks. The npm gate correctly refused native branch coverage 99.85% against unchanged 100%; Bun gates were skipped and are not passes. Added direct registered-handler format/refusal/positional cases to cover the new branches independently of child CLI processes. Targeted registered-handler installed/no-Git acceptance passed 1/1 and test typecheck passed. Full gates will rerun on the coverage fix."
  "2026-10-23T15:07:35.232Z",codex-agent,"CodeQL review identified nested-repeat backtracking in JSON Pointer validation. Replaced it with a linear disjoint-alternative pattern and checked the 256-character limit before matching. Added a child-process adversarial slash-run regression whose deadline starts after imports: the previous regex fails 0/1 at the five-second deadline; the restored validator passes 1/1. Source build/typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint passed. A direct global-JSON handler assertion addresses the sole remaining new-command branch from second CI (403/403 tests passed in both jobs, native branches 99.95%, gates correctly refused; no skipped Bun gate is counted). Final public-copy rerun on the linear validator: unchanged 87 items, 925 history events, 181 files, 87 current claims/0 pairs and 169 stale-history claims/82 pairs; witness size 2, JSON/TOON 691/773 bytes. Check times 36.93/71.77 ms, read/selection 3131.45 ms."
  "2026-10-23T15:07:56.873Z",codex-agent,Final local suite after pointer hardening passed 10/10 with 100% witness-module lines/branches/functions. The direct registered-handler/global-JSON installed no-Git scenario also passed its final targeted run 1/1. The README now explicitly identifies both --changed and --files as Git-requiring focus modes. Source and built validator match; full npm/Bun gate evidence remains pending the next CI head.
  "2026-10-23T15:18:43.701Z",codex-agent,"Third CI at 98d3bfc passed 404/404 tests and CodeQL, but the npm gate still reports one uncovered branch on the format fallback in index.ts; Bun gates are skipped, not passes. Expanded the registered-handler matrix to execute both the source extension and committed distribution in-process, including direct global JSON, explicit TOON, invalid format, absent packet and extra positional cases. This validates both delivered surfaces and avoids relying on coverage collected from spawned CLI processes. A targeted native-coverage probe is running before the next push."
  "2026-10-23T15:22:49.639Z",codex-agent,"Targeted native-coverage probe passed 1/1 against both source and committed distribution. Its LCOV now shows every new format/refusal branch at index.ts lines 1608-1609 hit, including the previously absent default-TOON branch. Direct handler contexts explicitly cover global JSON false with no format override as well as global JSON true. Refusal assertions now use the SDK isPmCliExpectedError cross-module guard instead of source-class identity. Test typecheck passed. Other index paths were deliberately outside this targeted probe; the unchanged full CI gates will verify the entire measured scope."
  "2026-10-23T15:32:47.104Z",codex-agent,"Verified full release gates at 068f747: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/actions/runs/39977973332 . Both Node 22 and Node 26 jobs passed npm run release:check and bun run release:check: 404/404 tests in each of four gates (1616 passing executions total), zero failures, skips, cancellations or todos. Native gate reported all 12 required source files with 100% lines/branches/functions. c8 reported 100% statements/lines/functions and 99.95% branches, above the unchanged 99.9% c8 branch threshold; this is not a claim of four-dimensional global 100%. Strict tracker health, fresh dist verification, changelog, dependency audit, package and publish-attestation checks passed. CodeQL passed the hardened implementation. Releasing the claim for orchestrator review; item remains in progress. A final tracker-evidence commit will receive its own CI run; final head/run link and counts are maintained in PR 168."
